WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>Sometimes, when Koizumi-san 
is around, I think that...</i>

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>ramen is...</i>

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.300
<i>Ramen is...</i>

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.620
Big Bro!

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.870
You can use the bath now.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.790
Sure, I'll go in after this.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.320
Don't you have classes 
early tomorrow morning?

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.400
Just go, before the water gets cold.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.410
My first period lecture got canceled.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.130
Goodnight, then.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.750
Goodnight.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.480
<b>October 3rd</b>

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.210
<i>October 3rd.</i>

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.110
<i>Today, Koizumi-san was eating...</i>

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:58.030
<i>some kind of pale blue-colored ramen.</i>

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:16.510
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.050
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:17.970
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.860
Welcome.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.000
<b>Ramen With Unknown Flavor</b>

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.760
Here you go.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.770
<i>The colors totally reminded me of 
some kind of Western cartoon monster.</i>

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.300
<i>I couldn't help but feel nervous 
when I looked at it.</i>

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.180
What is this soup's base, exactly?

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.960
Poison! Pure poison.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:02.910
P-Poison?!

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.510
I'm joking.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.690
Jeez, don't scare me like that.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.500
<i>Halfway through, Koizumi-san 
added some vinegar.</i>

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.100
<i>After she did that,
something strange happened.</i>

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.340
<i>The pale blue of the soup turned
into a pink like strawberry milk.</i>

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.110
<i>I had no idea what was going on.</i>

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.140
<i>But...</i>

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.600
<i>She looked really happy.</i>

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.800
<i>So I guess it must've been good.</i>

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.500
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.200
<i>By the way, I ordered the cocoa ramen.</i>

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.120
<i>You might think that's just
chocolate fondue with noodles,</i>

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.710
<i>but there could be no doubt that it was ramen!</i>

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.130
<i>But there was a faint cocoa aftertaste.</i>

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.530
Hey, what flavor is that ramen?

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.280
Before, it tasted light blue.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.720
Now, it tastes pink.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.600
Huh? What kind of flavor is that?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.500
Can I try a taste of the soup?

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.390
I didn't say anything.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.900
<i>Today's conversation went pretty well.</i>

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:22.190
Please! Find it in your heart 
to let me accompany you!

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.080
Please! I'm on my knees!

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.410
<i>I'm so glad we went together.</i>

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:33.160
<i>But sometimes, when I'm with Koizumi-san,
I catch myself thinking...</i>

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.920
<b>Blue Ramen
Yellow Ramen
Red Ramen
Light Blue Ramen
Purple Ramen
Char Siu Ramen
Miso Ramen</b>

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.670
<i>Yellow?</i>

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.920
<i>Blue?</i>

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.920
<b>Milk Ramen
Coffee Milk Ramen
Cocoa Ramen
Soy Milk Ramen
Natto Ramen</b>

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.570
<i>Soy milk?</i>

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:40.920
<i>Coffee milk?</i>

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.430
<b>Green Onion Ramen
Alkali ramen
Yam and Konbu Ramen
Milk Ramen
Coffee Milk Ramen
Cocoa Ramen
Soy Milk Ramen
Natto Ramen
Healthy Tea Ramen</b>

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.430
<i>Alkali?!</i>

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.550
<i>Ramen is...</i>

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.500
<i>the universe.</i>

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.690
<b>Blue?
Soy milk?
Alkali?!
is... the universe...</b>

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.450
<b>Koizumi-san Observation Log Vol. 2</b>

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.970
Huh?

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:31.140
<i>She's really been studying hard lately.</i>

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.520
<i>Maybe I should take her 
out for something tasty.</i>

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.360
<i>Payday's coming up.</i>

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.870
<b>Green Onion Ramen
Alkali ramen
Yam and Konbu Ramen
Milk Ramen
Coffee Milk Ramen
Cocoa Ramen
Soy Milk Ramen</b>

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.660
<b>Ramen really is the universe...</b>

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.950
What the heck is alkali ramen?

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:59.590
Apparently, they put these in soy sauce ramen.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.380
<b>Alkali</b>

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.380
<b>Alkali</b>

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.880
<b>Alkali</b>

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.880
<b>Alkali</b>

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.880
Batteries?!

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.040
<b>For real?</b>

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.500
For real?

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.810
That was a joke.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.380
<b>The actual flavor is
pickled plum</b>

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.390
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.220
Fried chicken with fries...

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.520
Pollock roe salad... and a mille crêpe.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.270
Mont blancs are good, too.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:22.610
You know...

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.150
You should be eating sushi.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:31.160
Sushiya

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.660
This is a sushi restaurant.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.160
<b>Conveyor Belt Ramen</b>

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.380
<i>My brother got paid today.</i>

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.910
<i>He uncharacteristically 
invited me out for dinner.</i>

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.690
You're the one who recommended this place.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.670
Well, it's fun because the menu 
has so many different choices!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.670
You can eat all kinds of things.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.490
Look, egg sushi!

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:51.390
This is my favorite!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.800
You child.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.190
What are you talking about?

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.920
Starting with egg is the in-thing.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.720
It said so online.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.200
Just shut up and have some fish.

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:03.820
Says the person who just took a tuna and mayo!

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:07.610
Tuna is a fish, and it happens 
to be one of my favorites.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:14.020
But shouldn't you be inviting your 
girlfriend to dinner on your payday?

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.720
Oh, wait, you don't have 
a girlfriend right now?

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.620
Wait, you haven't had one in forever?

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.740
That's it. We're splitting the bill.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.000
Just kidding! Sorry!

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:27.300
Okay, let's go for the salmon, 
to do this place justice.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.930
<i>Koizumi-san?!</i>

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.480
Do you know her?

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.390
Y-Yeah! She's my friend!

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.560
<i>No, more like my best friend! My bosom buddy!</i>

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.520
<i>Meeting in a place like this means we 
might even be destined to be soulmates.</i>

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.380
<i>But what is Koizumi-san doing at a conveyor 
belt sushi place, instead of a ramen place?</i>

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.030
<b>Japanese</b>

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.030
<b>How to Use      Allergens</b>

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.240
<b>Order</b>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.990
<i>And it looks like she knows this place well!</i>

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:01.410
A meal set?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.420
Time to eat.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.010
Her main dish is ramen after all!

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:34.990
<i>I see! Right now...</i>

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:44.990
<i>Koizumi-san is enjoying a special 
ramen she can only get here.</i>

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.130
<i>Even from behind, I can tell.</i>

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.400
<i>I want to go talk to her, 
but she's not here for that,</i>

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.510
<i>and just watching her is enough.</i>

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:56.460
Stare...

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.730
Stare...

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:01.770
<i>Brother?!</i>

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.890
<i>D-D-Don't tell me he also 
thinks Koizumi-san is...</i>

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:11.000
<i>No, I don't want to be competing for 
Koizumi-san with my own brother!</i>

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.740
<i>It's not fair! I was her friend first!</i>

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.440
<i>I was her friend first!</i>

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.070
<i>I was first!</i>

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:18.770
<i>I was first!</i>

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:19.440
<i>I was first!</i>

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.500
<i>I was first!</i>

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.340
Hey, I want to have ramen, too!

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.440
What about you?

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.160
<i>Safe!</i>

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:30.300
Wow, these all look good.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.550
<b>Order</b>

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:31.550
And they're cheap!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.720
Let's try them all.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.140
If we split them, we can
 finish them, right? Right?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.970
I'm glad you're my brother.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.970
<b>No</b>

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.970
<b>Lust</b>

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:45.400
I'm glad you've finally realized the 
awesomeness of your own brother.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.690
You can eat all you want today.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.190
I will.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.660
Time to eat!

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.530
<i>A ramen I can only experience here...</i>

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:46.290
<i>This is the best!</i>

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:49.790
Wait a minute...

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.700
Now that I look closer...

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.050
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.790
<i>Koizumi-san is my friend.</i>

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:57.840
<i>Koizumi-san is mine...</i>

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.400
<i>Mine, mine, mine, mine...</i>

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.890
That girl ate three bowls 
of ramen by herself.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.180
That's pretty amazing!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.560
Yeah, it is.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.160
It really is amazing.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:21.540
Ramen at conveyor belt sushi restaurants
often uses a seafood base for its soup,

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.500
which means it pairs perfectly with sushi.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.990
The deliciousness will make 
you dance involuntarily.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.990
<b>Accepting Challenges!!</b>

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:35.990
Hey, Koizumi-san!

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.510
Are you free today? Let's go out!

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.630
No.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.050
Oh, don't be like that.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.510
I'll pass.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.930
Yup, this is the cutest angle for me.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.140
But Yuu sure doesn't give up, huh?

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.400
She really doesn't.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.590
Let's go, Koizumi-san!

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.400
No.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.650
<b>Mom</b>

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.650
Mom?

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.170
Hello?

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.650
What? Today? Right now?

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.200
<i>Yes.</i>

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.440
<i>The department made a reservation, 
but now I can't go.</i>

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.950
<i>And the reservation can't 
be canceled, either.</i>

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.920
But I can't just...

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.560
<i>I'll take care of the bill,
so thanks, Jun-chan.</i>

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:18.250
<i>Bye.</i>

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.530
Mom?!

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.590
What's wrong?

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:29.310
Uh, can I talk to all of you for a minute?

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:31.820
If possible, Koizumi-san, too.

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.960
<b>Kagurazaka Hanten
Giant Fried Rice
Jumbo Gyoza
Accepting Challenges!!</b>

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:41.800
So you're saying you want us all to help you 
eat the special dinner your mom ordered.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:45.950
Sorry about this... But she said 
the more people, the better.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:49.950
If there's anything else you want, 
feel free to order it.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:54.280
Chinese food is always best 
when everyone's sharing.

00:12:55.360 --> 00:13:00.680
But it's ultra rare for the four 
of us to be eating out together.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:02.320
You're right.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:06.320
In fact, she turned me 
down when I invited her,

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:08.920
but she said yes when Jun asked...

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.200
So annoying.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.600
Sorry, I guess.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:17.310
It's all-you-can-eat ramen with the class rep
paying. Therefore, I'll take a tantanmen.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.860
Chinese Restaurant
||
Has Ramen
||
All-You-Can-Eat
Ramen

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.860
That was fast!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:22.800
That's right! That's so you, Koizumi-san.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.880
Wait, I don't know what 
they're going to bring out,

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.960
so let's see what we get first...

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:28.670
Thank you for waiting.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.860
Our special jumbo gyoza.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.880
Whoa! What is that?!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.250
It's huge!

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:43.100
This is so funny!

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.630
That's amazing. It's like a pillow.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:50.140
Wait, so is this what she meant by "special"?

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:53.900
This is supposed to be the equivalent 
of 100 regular gyoza, which means...

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:58.200
Using simple math, we'd 
have to eat 25 gyoza each!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.480
We'll... get through it somehow.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:06.850
The skin looks pretty thick, though. 
So if you take that into account...

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:10.280
I should've brought some more people.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.280
Excuse me. I'd like to order one of these.

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:15.340
Hello! Do you not see what's going on?!

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:17.400
Why are you ordering even more?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.980
We can't eat ramen on top of this!

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:22.570
I'll be eating the ramen by myself.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.790
Of course, I'll have some 
of the gyoza, as well.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.050
Are you for real?

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.050
Eating at a Chinese restaurant 
naturally means gyoza and ramen.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:33.760
Well, it is Koizumi-san.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.980
All right, I'm going to divide it up.

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.160
Fight, Yuu!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.270
Here I go.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:42.230
<i>Of course!</i>

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.150
<i>If I ask Koizumi-san to help me with this...</i>

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:59.860
<i>It'll be our chance to complete our 
very first cooperative activity!</i>

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:08.300
You know, this is pretty 
hard to cut by myself.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:12.450
Sorry, but could you help me, Koizumi-san?

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:13.350
Sure.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:18.060
<i>Our first cooperative activity!</i>

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.660
Look at that meat juice!

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:26.820
It looks good.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.440
That's not what I had in mind...

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.450
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.280
Here's one jumbo ramen and one tantanmen.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:38.680
Jumbo ramen?

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.280
What the heck did you order?!

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.440
Wow.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.140
Our table is in chaos.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.590
It's messing with my depth perception.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:47.960
Time to eat.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.920
We should just start eating, too.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:59.720
R-Right.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:01.350
Time to eat!

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.190
It's like a gyoza cake!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:07.290
First, try it with a little
bit of the sauce...

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:15.200
The skin is almost like bread!
It's so thick and chewy!

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.660
Oh, yeah! It's like the gyoza 
version of roasted mochi!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.790
This is so good, I think we can eat it all.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.820
Do you mind if I get a shungiku ramen?

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:35.510
S-Sure, that's fine...

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.390
I'm covering my next piece with chili oil.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.600
Isn't that too much?

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.240
I'll try mine with vinegar.

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.190
Thank you for waiting.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.200
Here's your shungiku ramen.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:52.690
That smells so good.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.340
It does.

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:57.880
So, Koizumi-san, what kind of ramen is that?

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:00.320
It tastes like shungiku.

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.950
Like shungiku?

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.910
That's literally the name.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:04.960
It looks good.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.810
The aroma of the fat goes 
really well with the soup.

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:09.810
It's ramen that tastes like shungiku.

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:12.600
If you're curious, we can order another one.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:13.900
Yeah, let's do that!

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.360
What? No, no!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.720
If we order more, we won't 
be able to finish it all!

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:22.720
I'm getting so full.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.480
We're all slowing down quite a bit.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:27.380
I could keep going.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.480
Really? That's not like you.

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.130
You used to have such a small appetite.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.580
Look at you now.

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:36.700
Maybe it's because I've been going 
out to eat with Koizumi-san.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.440
A char siu ramen, please.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.200
What? You're ordering more?

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.520
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.330
<b>Kagurazaka Hanten</b>

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:52.340
Incredible.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.000
I'll take a gomoku soba.

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:58.480
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:11.360
We can't just sit here and be impressed.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.140
Right.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.300
M-Me, either!

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:51.500
I give up!

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.640
I'm so full.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:56.630
Me, too. This is my limit for enjoying food.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.000
Same here.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:01.160
Maybe I should order a drink.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.090
They have a jumbo ramen 
eating contest here!

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:07.600
Koizumi-san should've entered!

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:08.870
Oh, yeah.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:12.830
I guess this gyoza was originally 
made for their eating competition.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:16.170
Too bad we noticed too late, huh, Koizumi?

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:19.800
I knew about their challenge menu,

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.680
but I'm not really into competitive eating.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.480
Why not?

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.180
Is it the time limit?

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:35.940
I just don't think I can eat enough to 
enter such an event with any confidence.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.470
<i>No self-awareness at all...</i>

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.420
<i>Scary...</i>

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:45.760
Class Rep, may I order a mapo ramen next?

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.270
And if there's any gyoza left, I'll take it.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:50.210
Uh, sure.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.170
Thank you!

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:56.400
That was so good.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.540
So good, I overate.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.590
Me, too. I can't eat another bite.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:08.180
Koizumi-san? What's wrong?

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:11.730
Huh?

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.520
What's up?

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.930
This would be okay, too.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:24.330
I don't even want to hear 
about gyoza right now!

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:26.370
<b>|

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:29.160
My mom incredulously asked 
how many people I took.

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:30.870
That's Koizumi.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.400
That's Koizumi-san!

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.000
That's Koizumi-san!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Tasty Ramen</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Osaka</b>

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:13.110
That jumbo gyoza sure was something.

00:22:13.110 --> 00:22:15.070
It was supposed to be 100 servings of gyoza.

00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:18.140
We filled up almost exclusively 
on the gyoza, but Koizumi-san,

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:20.120
how many bowls of ramen
did you end up eating?

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:23.840
Yeah! It's not fair that you can eat 
that much and not gain weight!

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.970
You'd better give up your secret right now!

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:26.870
I don't know what to say.

00:22:26.870 --> 00:22:29.510
She's an angel! That's why
she doesn't gain weight!

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:36.000
<b>Thank you for the meal!</b>
